# Build output. tvDownloadOHLC once tracked ninjatrader-addon/obj/ and a
# RiskGuardTests.exe; that is what P2-28 was about. Do not repeat it.
bin/
obj/
*.exe
*.pdb
*.user

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Mutation batteries restore the file they edit, but a crashed run can leave this.
*.mutation_backup

# agent-loop per-run artifacts: prompts, raw model output, per-round build/test
# logs, the candidate patch, and the .runlock a crashed run leaves behind.
# NOTE the `/*` rather than `/`: git never descends into an excluded DIRECTORY,
# so a negation under `logs/agent_loop/` would be silently impossible. `/*`
# excludes the contents while still allowing the exceptions below. Same rule and
# same reason as tvDownloadOHLC's.
logs/agent_loop/*
# These two ARE tracked, deliberately: they are cross-machine run history that
# the loop itself reads back, not per-run artifacts. `report` mode reads the
# ledger and `docs --docs-type handover` builds on it, so dropping them would
# silently reset that history on a fresh clone.
!logs/agent_loop/ledger.jsonl
!logs/agent_loop/learning_feedback.jsonl
